name: "FauciPaulHearingFull"

# ============================================================================
# THE FAUCI / PAUL HEARING -- Senate Homeland Security and Governmental
# Affairs Committee, July 29 2026.
#
# A real, live, contested public dispute mapped into the tool's structure.
# The scenario takes no side. Both positions are entered as claims with their
# strongest supporting material, and the tool declares no winner -- which is
# the entire point of the design.
#
# BACKGROUND (verified against reporting, July-August 2026)
#   - Paul, committee chairman, subpoenaed Fauci in June 2026 after Fauci
#     withdrew from a voluntary testimony agreement.
#   - Ahead of the hearing Paul released 1,100+ pages of Fauci's personal
#     journals covering December 2019 to December 2022. HHS Secretary
#     Kennedy said the records were recovered from 11 government servers over
#     eight months and handed to Paul and Sen. Johnson. Neither HHS nor the
#     committee notified Fauci before publication.
#   - At the hearing Fauci invoked the Fifth Amendment and declined to answer
#     any questions. He now faces a contempt vote.
#   - The long-running charge concerns Fauci's May 2021 testimony: "The NIH
#     has not ever and does not now fund gain-of-function research in the
#     Wuhan Institute of Virology."
#
# WHY THIS CASE
#   It stacks five mechanisms a naive argument tool gets wrong:
#     1. A definitional dispute that decides a factual verdict
#     2. Evidence that is undisputed but whose INFERENCE is disputed
#     3. Provenance attacks that must not touch what a document says
#     4. Refusal to engage -- silence that is neither concession nor defeat
#     5. Independent supports where defeating one must not defeat the rest
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WHAT THE ENGINE CANNOT EXPRESS  (see section 6 of the scenario guide)
#
#   [SUB-A] OPPOSE targeting a RELATION.
#      Fauci's real move against the journals is "the entries are genuine,
#      your inference from them fails." That attacks the link, and should
#      yield UNSUPPORTED with the evidence untouched. Only claims can be
#      targeted, so every such move below is substituted with a claim-level
#      challenge -- strictly STRONGER than the case warrants.
#
#   [GAP-B] CONTESTED. Several branches here have real surviving support on
#      both sides and no winner. With three statuses there is no way to
#      say so.
#
#   [GAP-C] UNSUPPORTED and relation states. When a member of a multi-from
#      relation is conceded, that relation should go INERT and its target
#      should become UNSUPPORTED -- not proven, not disproven, revivable.
#      Not expressible.
#
#   [GAP-D] Lenses. The gain-of-function verdict should flip with the
#      reader's choice of definition, writing nothing. Here the definition is
#      instead settled by concession, which is a different and cruder thing.
#
#   [GAP-E] The author lane. Credibility and provenance attacks must be fully
#      debatable while being STRUCTURALLY INCAPABLE of changing a claim's
#      truth. There is no lane, so the provenance challenge below wrongly
#      threatens the evidence it targets.
#
#   [GAP-F] The origin question itself (lab incident vs natural spillover) is
#      DELIBERATELY OMITTED. It is the CONTESTED case in its purest form --
#      an intelligence community split, no resolution, records unavailable.
#      Modelling it here would either fake a winner or hang it beneath a
#      claim it is not a sub-claim of. It needs its own scenario once
#      CONTESTED exists.
#
#   [GAP-G] REST / ACCEPT / REOPEN / TIMEOUT. Notably there is no way to
#      express that Fauci declined to engage at all -- see BRANCH D.
#
# CLAIM IDS are sequential and noted beside every action. 23 claims total.
# ============================================================================

steps { action { username: "paul"  event_type: "CREATE_USER" } }
steps { action { username: "fauci" event_type: "CREATE_USER" } }

# claim 1 -- the root accusation
steps {
  action {
    username: "paul"
    event_type: "CREATE_DEBATE"
    debate_topic: "Fauci was dishonest with Congress and the public about COVID-19"
  }
}

steps { action { username: "paul"  event_type: "JOIN_DEBATE"  debate_id: 1 } }
steps { action { username: "paul"  event_type: "ENTER_DEBATE" debate_id: 1 } }
steps { action { username: "fauci" event_type: "JOIN_DEBATE"  debate_id: 1 } }
steps { action { username: "fauci" event_type: "ENTER_DEBATE" debate_id: 1 } }

steps {
  expectations { check_type: "CLAIM_EXISTS" claim_id: 1 }
  expectations { check_type: "COLLECTION_SIZE" expected_count: 1 }
  expectations { check_type: "ENGAGEMENT_STATE" username: "paul"  expected_action: "ACTION_DEBATING" }
  expectations { check_type: "ENGAGEMENT_STATE" username: "fauci" expected_action: "ACTION_DEBATING" }
}

# ============================================================================
# BRANCH A -- did his public statements differ from his private view?
#
# Tests: a multi-from relation, a provenance attack, independent support.
# ============================================================================

# claim 2 -- first of FOUR independent supports for the root.
# Each of the four is a separate relation. Defeating one must leave the
# others standing. This is the OR case, asserted after the concessions.
steps { action { username: "paul" event_type: "GO_TO_CLAIM" claim_id: 1 } }
steps {
  action {
    username: "paul"
    event_type: "ADD_CHILD_CLAIM"
    claim_text: "Fauci's public statements about the virus's origin differed from his private view"
    basis: "EVIDENTIAL"
  }
}

# claims 3 and 4 -- ONE relation, TWO from-claims, JOINTLY required.
# The private record alone shows only uncertainty, which is not dishonesty.
# The public statement alone shows only a stated position. Only the two
# TOGETHER support a divergence claim. This is why from_claim_ids is a list.
steps { action { username: "paul" event_type: "GO_TO_CLAIM" claim_id: 2 } }
steps {
  action {
    username: "paul"
    event_type: "ADD_CHILD_CLAIM"
    claim_text: "Fauci's journals from December 2019 to December 2022 record uncertainty about the origin of the virus"
    extra_claim_texts: "Early in the pandemic Fauci publicly said the evidence pointed very, very strongly toward a natural origin"
    basis: "EVIDENTIAL"
  }
}

steps {
  expectations { check_type: "COLLECTION_SIZE" expected_count: 4 }
  expectations { check_type: "RELATION_FROM_COUNT" to_claim_id: 2 expected_count: 2 }
  expectations { check_type: "RELATION_FROM_EXISTS" from_claim_id: 3 to_claim_id: 2 }
  expectations { check_type: "RELATION_FROM_EXISTS" from_claim_id: 4 to_claim_id: 2 }
  expectations { check_type: "USER_VIEW" claim_id: 3 username: "paul" expected_status: "TRUE_CLAIM" }
  expectations { check_type: "USER_VIEW" claim_id: 4 username: "paul" expected_status: "TRUE_CLAIM" }
}

# claim 5 -- [GAP-E] the provenance attack.
#
# This targets HOW the journals were obtained, not WHAT THEY SAY. Authorship
# is not disputed by anyone. In the target design this belongs in the author
# lane: fully debatable, capable of flagging the source's handling, and
# STRUCTURALLY UNABLE to change claim 3's truth.
#
# With no lane it becomes an ordinary challenge, which wrongly puts the
# journals' contents at risk. If claim 3 ever flips to FALSE_CLAIM as a
# result, that is the lane's absence doing damage -- not a correct outcome.
steps { action { username: "fauci" event_type: "GO_TO_CLAIM" claim_id: 3 } }
steps {
  action {
    username: "fauci"
    event_type: "SUBMIT_CHALLENGE_CLAIM"
    claim_text: "The journals were recovered from government servers by HHS and published by the committee without notifying Fauci beforehand"
    challenge_description: "Provenance and process, not content. Authorship is undisputed."
    basis: "AUTHORITY"
  }
}

# claim 6 -- a SECOND, independent support for claim 2.
# Separate ADD_CHILD_CLAIM on the same parent = separate relation = OR.
steps { action { username: "paul" event_type: "GO_TO_CLAIM" claim_id: 2 } }
steps {
  action {
    username: "paul"
    event_type: "ADD_CHILD_CLAIM"
    claim_text: "A released email shows Fauci directed a scientist to report furin cleavage site concerns to the FBI and MI5"
    basis: "EVIDENTIAL"
  }
}

# claim 7 -- [SUB-A] Fauci's counter.
# His actual position is that the inference fails, not that the record is
# false: stating a leading hypothesis publicly while noting uncertainty
# privately is ordinary scientific caution. That is an attack on the LINK
# from [3,4] to 2. Rendered here as a claim-level challenge.
steps { action { username: "fauci" event_type: "GO_TO_CLAIM" claim_id: 2 } }
steps {
  action {
    username: "fauci"
    event_type: "SUBMIT_CHALLENGE_CLAIM"
    claim_text: "Stating a leading hypothesis in public while recording uncertainty in private is not a contradiction"
    challenge_description: "The journals are genuine. The inference from them does not follow."
    basis: "EVIDENTIAL"
  }
}

steps {
  expectations { check_type: "COLLECTION_SIZE" expected_count: 7 }
  # claim 2 now has TWO separate supporting relations -- [3,4] and [6]
  expectations { check_type: "RELATION_FROM_EXISTS" from_claim_id: 6 to_claim_id: 2 }
  expectations { check_type: "RELATION_COUNT" link_type: "CHALLENGE" expected_count: 2 }
}

# ============================================================================
# BRANCH B -- the perjury charge, and the definition it turns on
#
# The heart of the case. The underlying facts are agreed by both parties.
# The verdict depends entirely on what "gain-of-function" means.
# ============================================================================

# claim 8 -- second independent support for the root
steps { action { username: "paul" event_type: "GO_TO_CLAIM" claim_id: 1 } }
steps {
  action {
    username: "paul"
    event_type: "ADD_CHILD_CLAIM"
    claim_text: "Fauci's May 2021 denial that NIH funded gain-of-function research at the Wuhan Institute was false"
    basis: "EVIDENTIAL"
  }
}

# claims 9, 10, 11 -- ONE relation, THREE from-claims, the third a DEFINITION.
#
# THE CENTRAL MECHANISM OF THIS SCENARIO.
#
# Claims 9 and 10 are not in dispute -- both sides agree the grant existed
# and agree what Fauci said. They establish "the denial was false" ONLY
# under a particular reading of the term. Putting the definition inside the
# from-set is what makes the equivocation visible: change claim 11 and the
# same undisputed facts stop supporting the accusation.
#
# In prose this is invisible, because the phrase "gain-of-function" looks
# constant while doing different work on each side.
steps { action { username: "paul" event_type: "GO_TO_CLAIM" claim_id: 8 } }
steps {
  action {
    username: "paul"
    event_type: "ADD_CHILD_CLAIM"
    claim_text: "NIAID awarded a grant to EcoHealth Alliance that included a sub-award to the Wuhan Institute of Virology"
    extra_claim_texts: "In May 2021 Senate testimony Fauci said the NIH has not ever and does not now fund gain-of-function research in the Wuhan Institute of Virology"
    extra_claim_texts: "Gain-of-function research means any research that enhances a viral property such as transmissibility or virulence"
    basis: "EVIDENTIAL"
  }
}

steps {
  expectations { check_type: "COLLECTION_SIZE" expected_count: 11 }
  expectations { check_type: "RELATION_FROM_COUNT" to_claim_id: 8 expected_count: 3 }
  expectations { check_type: "RELATION_FROM_EXISTS" from_claim_id: 9  to_claim_id: 8 }
  expectations { check_type: "RELATION_FROM_EXISTS" from_claim_id: 10 to_claim_id: 8 }
  expectations { check_type: "RELATION_FROM_EXISTS" from_claim_id: 11 to_claim_id: 8 }
  expectations { check_type: "CLAIM_SENTENCE" claim_id: 11
                 expected_claim_sentence: "Gain-of-function research means any research that enhances a viral property such as transmissibility or virulence" }
}

# claim 12 -- Fauci challenges the DEFINITION, conceding both facts.
# This is the honest shape of his position: he does not dispute the grant or
# his own words, only the meaning of the term he was asked about.
#
# The basis matters most here of anywhere in the file. Fauci disputes no
# fact -- only what the term covers -- and DEFINITIONAL is what records that
# "you are wrong about the word" is a different move from "you are wrong
# about the world". Without it the engine stores both identically.
steps { action { username: "fauci" event_type: "GO_TO_CLAIM" claim_id: 11 } }
steps {
  action {
    username: "fauci"
    event_type: "SUBMIT_CHALLENGE_CLAIM"
    claim_text: "The governing federal standard is enhanced potential pandemic pathogen, meaning a pathogen already highly transmissible and virulent in humans that has been made more so"
    challenge_description: "The applicable definition is the federal one, not a general one."
    basis: "DEFINITIONAL"
  }
}

# claims 13, 14 -- AUTHORITY-basis support for the narrow definition
steps { action { username: "fauci" event_type: "GO_TO_CLAIM" claim_id: 12 } }
steps {
  action {
    username: "fauci"
    event_type: "ADD_CHILD_CLAIM"
    claim_text: "In 2017 federal officials replaced the 2014 to 2017 funding pause with enhanced scrutiny for enhanced potential pandemic pathogens"
    extra_claim_texts: "NIH stated in 2021 that the Wuhan studies did not require that extra review because they involved bat coronaviruses genetically distant from the pandemic virus"
    basis: "AUTHORITY"
  }
}

# claim 15 -- Paul's counter to the NIH position
steps { action { username: "paul" event_type: "GO_TO_CLAIM" claim_id: 14 } }
steps {
  action {
    username: "paul"
    event_type: "SUBMIT_CHALLENGE_CLAIM"
    claim_text: "The funded experiments produced chimeric viruses that do not occur in nature and showed increased pathogenicity in animal models"
    challenge_description: "Whatever the label, the function was enhanced."
    basis: "EVIDENTIAL"
  }
}

# claim 16 -- a second independent support for claim 8.
# Fauci himself called the term unsettled, which cuts against resting on a
# narrow reading of it.
steps { action { username: "paul" event_type: "GO_TO_CLAIM" claim_id: 8 } }
steps {
  action {
    username: "paul"
    event_type: "ADD_CHILD_CLAIM"
    claim_text: "Fauci described the term gain-of-function as very nebulous in 2021 testimony"
    basis: "EVIDENTIAL"
  }
}

steps {
  expectations { check_type: "COLLECTION_SIZE" expected_count: 16 }
  expectations { check_type: "RELATION_FROM_COUNT" to_claim_id: 12 expected_count: 2 }
  expectations { check_type: "RELATION_FROM_EXISTS" from_claim_id: 13 to_claim_id: 12 }
  expectations { check_type: "RELATION_FROM_EXISTS" from_claim_id: 14 to_claim_id: 12 }
  expectations { check_type: "RELATION_FROM_EXISTS" from_claim_id: 16 to_claim_id: 8 }
  expectations { check_type: "RELATION_COUNT" link_type: "CHALLENGE" expected_count: 4 }
}

# ============================================================================
# BRANCH C -- who actually made the funding decision
#
# A framing dispute. The money reached Wuhan; the characterisation of how is
# contested.
# ============================================================================

# claim 17 -- third independent support for the root
steps { action { username: "paul" event_type: "GO_TO_CLAIM" claim_id: 1 } }
steps {
  action {
    username: "paul"
    event_type: "ADD_CHILD_CLAIM"
    claim_text: "Fauci chose to fund dangerous research in China"
    basis: "EVIDENTIAL"
  }
}

# claim 18 -- the counter
steps { action { username: "fauci" event_type: "GO_TO_CLAIM" claim_id: 17 } }
steps {
  action {
    username: "fauci"
    event_type: "SUBMIT_CHALLENGE_CLAIM"
    claim_text: "NIAID funds reached the Wuhan Institute through a sub-award administered by EcoHealth Alliance rather than a direct funding decision by Fauci"
    challenge_description: "The money arriving is not in dispute. The word chose is."
    basis: "DEFINITIONAL"
  }
}

# ============================================================================
# BRANCH D -- the Fifth Amendment
#
# The most structurally interesting part of the hearing, and the part the
# engine handles worst.
#
# Fauci answered nothing. In the target design silence is its own outcome:
# ABANDONED, recording WHO went quiet, explicitly distinct from concession
# and explicitly distinct from defeat. Here there is no way to represent
# "declined to engage" at all -- so Paul's inference from the silence is
# entered as an ordinary claim and Fauci's objection as an ordinary
# challenge, which makes a constitutional question look like a factual one.
# ============================================================================

# claim 19 -- fourth independent support for the root
steps { action { username: "paul" event_type: "GO_TO_CLAIM" claim_id: 1 } }
steps {
  action {
    username: "paul"
    event_type: "ADD_CHILD_CLAIM"
    claim_text: "Fauci's refusal to answer under oath indicates he could not answer truthfully"
    basis: "EVIDENTIAL"
  }
}

# claims 20, 21 -- ONE relation, TWO from-claims
steps { action { username: "paul" event_type: "GO_TO_CLAIM" claim_id: 19 } }
steps {
  action {
    username: "paul"
    event_type: "ADD_CHILD_CLAIM"
    claim_text: "At the July 29 2026 hearing Fauci invoked the Fifth Amendment and declined to answer the committee's questions"
    extra_claim_texts: "Senator Johnson said it would be almost impossible for Fauci to answer the questions truthfully without demonstrating what he did"
    basis: "EVIDENTIAL"
  }
}

# claim 22 -- the objection.
# Note this is a NORMATIVE / legal-principle claim, not a factual one: no
# evidence settles whether an inference from silence is legitimate. The
# engine has no way to mark that distinction on a challenge.
steps { action { username: "fauci" event_type: "GO_TO_CLAIM" claim_id: 19 } }
steps {
  action {
    username: "fauci"
    event_type: "SUBMIT_CHALLENGE_CLAIM"
    claim_text: "Invoking the Fifth Amendment is a constitutional right from which no inference of wrongdoing follows"
    challenge_description: "Silence under a right is not evidence."
    basis: "NORMATIVE"
  }
}

# claim 23 -- supporting context for the objection
steps { action { username: "fauci" event_type: "GO_TO_CLAIM" claim_id: 22 } }
steps {
  action {
    username: "fauci"
    event_type: "ADD_CHILD_CLAIM"
    claim_text: "Fauci's attorneys cited repeated public statements by the committee chairman that Fauci should be prosecuted and jailed"
    basis: "EVIDENTIAL"
  }
}

# ---- full structure assertion ---------------------------------------------
steps {
  expectations { check_type: "COLLECTION_SIZE" expected_count: 23 }
  expectations { check_type: "RELATION_COUNT" link_type: "PARENT_CHILD" expected_count: 11 }
  expectations { check_type: "RELATION_COUNT" link_type: "CHALLENGE"    expected_count: 6 }
  # the root's four independent supports
  expectations { check_type: "RELATION_FROM_EXISTS" from_claim_id: 2  to_claim_id: 1 }
  expectations { check_type: "RELATION_FROM_EXISTS" from_claim_id: 8  to_claim_id: 1 }
  expectations { check_type: "RELATION_FROM_EXISTS" from_claim_id: 17 to_claim_id: 1 }
  expectations { check_type: "RELATION_FROM_EXISTS" from_claim_id: 19 to_claim_id: 1 }
  expectations { check_type: "RELATION_FROM_COUNT" to_claim_id: 19 expected_count: 2 }
}

# ============================================================================
# CONCESSIONS
#
# CONCEDE_CHALLENGE takes no argument. The runner selects, among CHALLENGE
# links whose TARGET claim was created by the conceding user, the one with
# the HIGHEST challenging-claim id -- the most recent challenge against
# something that user said.
#
# Outstanding challenges against claims paul created:
#     claim 5  -> claim 3    (provenance)
#     claim 7  -> claim 2    (inference)
#     claim 12 -> claim 11   (the definition)
#     claim 18 -> claim 17   (chose to fund)
#     claim 22 -> claim 19   (the Fifth)
#
# So paul's concessions fire in this order: 22, 18, 12, 7, 5.
# ============================================================================

# --- concession 1: paul concedes that no inference follows from the Fifth ---
steps { action { username: "paul" event_type: "CONCEDE_CHALLENGE" } }

steps {
  expectations { check_type: "USER_VIEW" claim_id: 19 username: "paul" expected_status: "FALSE_CLAIM" }
  # THE OR TEST. Claim 19 was one of FOUR independent supports for the root.
  # Losing it must NOT disturb the other three, nor the evidence beneath it.
  expectations { check_type: "USER_VIEW" claim_id: 20 username: "paul" expected_status: "TRUE_CLAIM" }
  expectations { check_type: "USER_VIEW" claim_id: 21 username: "paul" expected_status: "TRUE_CLAIM" }
  expectations { check_type: "RELATION_FROM_EXISTS" from_claim_id: 2  to_claim_id: 1 }
  expectations { check_type: "RELATION_FROM_EXISTS" from_claim_id: 8  to_claim_id: 1 }
  expectations { check_type: "RELATION_FROM_EXISTS" from_claim_id: 17 to_claim_id: 1 }
  expectations { check_type: "COLLECTION_SIZE" expected_count: 23 }
}

# --- concession 2: paul concedes the "chose to fund" framing ---------------
steps { action { username: "paul" event_type: "CONCEDE_CHALLENGE" } }

steps {
  expectations { check_type: "USER_VIEW" claim_id: 17 username: "paul" expected_status: "FALSE_CLAIM" }
  expectations { check_type: "USER_VIEW" claim_id: 9  username: "paul" expected_status: "TRUE_CLAIM" }
}

# --- concession 3: paul concedes the broad definition ----------------------
#
# THE KEY MOVE. Claim 11 is a member of the three-source relation
# [9, 10, 11] -> 8. Conceding it removes the definition that made the two
# undisputed facts add up to an accusation.
steps { action { username: "paul" event_type: "CONCEDE_CHALLENGE" } }

steps {
  expectations { check_type: "USER_VIEW" claim_id: 11 username: "paul" expected_status: "FALSE_CLAIM" }
  # THE FACTS MUST SURVIVE. Neither party ever disputed the grant or the
  # testimony. If either of these flips, an attack on the DEFINITION has
  # leaked into the EVIDENCE -- a real failure, not a limitation.
  expectations { check_type: "USER_VIEW" claim_id: 9  username: "paul" expected_status: "TRUE_CLAIM" }
  expectations { check_type: "USER_VIEW" claim_id: 10 username: "paul" expected_status: "TRUE_CLAIM" }
  # the structure is unchanged by a concession
  expectations { check_type: "RELATION_FROM_COUNT" to_claim_id: 8 expected_count: 3 }
  # claim 16 is an independent support for claim 8 and must be untouched
  expectations { check_type: "USER_VIEW" claim_id: 16 username: "paul" expected_status: "TRUE_CLAIM" }
}

# [GAP-C] -- THE MOST IMPORTANT UNASSERTED RESULT IN THIS FILE.
#
# Claim 8 ("the denial was false") now rests on a relation one of whose three
# members is false. In the target design:
#     relation [9,10,11] -> 8   goes INERT
#     claim 8                   becomes UNSUPPORTED
# meaning: not proven and not disproven. Paul has not been shown wrong; he
# has been shown not to have established it under the definition that
# survived. And if the definition were reopened, the relation would revive
# on its own with no further action.
#
# With three statuses there is no way to say any of that. Whatever the engine
# reports for claim 8 after this step, RECORD IT -- the distance between that
# and UNSUPPORTED is the exact measure of what the status engine still owes.
#
# Deliberately NOT asserted: FALSE_CLAIM would bless the wrong answer,
# UNDETERMINED would be a guess.

# --- fauci concedes: the only challenge against a fauci-created claim ------
# claim 15 -> claim 14. Conceding removes the NIH position from the pair
# [13, 14] -> 12 supporting the narrow definition.
steps { action { username: "fauci" event_type: "CONCEDE_CHALLENGE" } }

steps {
  expectations { check_type: "USER_VIEW" claim_id: 14 username: "fauci" expected_status: "FALSE_CLAIM" }
  expectations { check_type: "USER_VIEW" claim_id: 13 username: "fauci" expected_status: "TRUE_CLAIM" }
  expectations { check_type: "RELATION_FROM_COUNT" to_claim_id: 12 expected_count: 2 }
  expectations { check_type: "COLLECTION_SIZE" expected_count: 23 }
}

# ============================================================================
# WHAT A PASS MEANS
#
# Structural: multi-from relations build and survive concession; a definition
# can sit inside a from-set; four independent relations coexist on one parent
# and defeating one leaves the rest; concession propagates without disturbing
# the graph; attacks on one member do not leak into its siblings.
#
# WHAT A PASS DOES NOT MEAN. Five of the mechanisms this hearing actually
# turns on are absent:
#
#   - the inference attack (Fauci's real position on the journals)
#   - CONTESTED (the origin question, omitted entirely)
#   - the definitional lens (settled here by concession instead)
#   - the author lane (provenance wrongly threatens content)
#   - silence as its own outcome, which is what the hearing WAS
#
# Every substitution above is cruder than the case requires. A green run
# certifies the plumbing, not the design.
# ============================================================================
